 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The sea journey is a parable of man, not a punishment: `sea` mood, a ship, then wind and waves for the storm; hands for the sincere prayer, leaving before «الله». No people drawn. Their vow (22:35-41) is not glossed. 23:19-25 is not glossed (Al-Muyassar's first-person «فنخبركم»). STAGING v4: c1 (22) is staged on a sea shore by day: a camel and three travellers come along the shore (He makes you travel by land and sea; Al-Muyassar: on mounts and in ships) and the travellers fade out beside the ship as 22:11 (the ship) is recited: they have boarded; the people aboard are not drawn after that. A gust on 22:14 (the good wind), then the storm from 22:19 (the stormy wind; nobody is hurt and the ship stays whole), a wave plate for the waves from every side (22:22). Their sincere du'a (22:30) is shown only by a hands plate that leaves on the Name (22:31); their vow (22:35-41) gets camera only. c2 (23) on the same shore, calm: the three men appear by the ship on 23:2 (He saved them) and walk inland on 23:5 (they transgress on the land; the gloss says they forgot the hardship and the du'a); nobody faces an empty side, no idol is implied. The admonition (23:10-25) gets camera moves on them and a falling-leaf plate for the brief enjoyment of this world (23:16). The cover now shows the ship in the storm (22:26)."
 },
